            {
                "box": {
                    "code": "// SSB Frequency Shifter (Bipolar & Seamless)\n// Inputs:\n//   in1: I (In-phase signal from hilbert~ left outlet)\n//   in2: Q (Quadrature signal from hilbert~ right outlet)\n//   in3: Delta F (Bipolar frequency shift in Hz)\n\nHistory phase(0);\n\ndf = in3; // Bipolar frequency shift in Hz\n\n// 1. Accumulate phase using a bipolar step\n// GenExpr's wrap() handles negative phases beautifully, allowing the phase \n// accumulator to smoothly stop, reverse direction, and wrap backward.\nphase_step = df / samplerate;\nphase = wrap(phase + phase_step, 0.0, 1.0);\n\n// 2. Generate the quadrature carrier oscillators\nc_cos = cos(phase * twopi);\nc_sin = sin(phase * twopi);\n\n// 3. Single-Sideband Modulation (Pop-Free & Unified)\n// Upward shift (df > 0):   I * cos(wt) + Q * sin(wt)\n// Downward shift (df < 0): I * cos(-wt) + Q * sin(-wt) = I * cos(wt) - Q * sin(wt)\n//\n// Because cos(-x) = cos(x) and sin(-x) = -sin(x), the bipolar phase step \n// automatically handles the sign inversion of the second term. \n// There is no branching, no step-functions, and absolutely no discontinuity!\nout1 = (in1 * c_cos) + (in2 * c_sin);\n",
                    "fontface": 0,
                    "fontname": "<Monospaced>",
                    "fontsize": 12.0,
                    "id": "obj-3",
                    "maxclass": "codebox",
                    "numinlets": 3,
                    "numoutlets": 1,
                    "outlettype": [ "" ],
                    "patching_rect": [ 110.0, 142.0, 589.0, 424.0 ]
                }
